WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.108 --> 00:00:04.201
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:04.201 --> 00:00:05.708
My name is Evan Carmichael,

00:00:05.708 --> 00:00:07.151
my one word is believe,

00:00:07.151 --> 00:00:09.150
and I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve all

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.130
of the major problems in the world.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.391
So, to help you on your journey,

00:00:12.391 --> 00:00:16.437
today we're going to talk about
how you can find your purpose.

00:00:16.437 --> 00:00:18.020
And as always as you're watching,

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.575
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:19.575 --> 00:00:21.006
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:00:21.006 --> 00:00:23.887
put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired,

00:00:23.887 --> 00:00:25.694
you might win a prize, too.

00:00:25.694 --> 00:00:26.869
And also, when you write it down,

00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:29.806
it's much more likely to
stick for yourself, as well.

00:00:29.806 --> 00:00:30.639
Enjoy.

00:00:31.514 --> 00:00:34.597
(upbeat intro music)

00:00:49.151 --> 00:00:51.395
- If I said to you that
you can have any one thing,

00:00:51.395 --> 00:00:53.229
you can have good health,

00:00:53.229 --> 00:00:54.799
you can have money,

00:00:54.799 --> 00:00:57.605
you can have the fame that
allows you to inspire people.

00:00:57.605 --> 00:01:00.965
What would you choose as a one thing?

00:01:00.965 --> 00:01:02.961
- Certainly, I think without
health, you're not around

00:01:02.961 --> 00:01:03.794
to do anything.

00:01:03.794 --> 00:01:04.693
But I think it's a life of meaning.

00:01:04.693 --> 00:01:06.178
I don't think, I know it is.

00:01:06.178 --> 00:01:07.807
Feeling like your life matters,

00:01:07.807 --> 00:01:10.066
because you've had the experience.

00:01:10.066 --> 00:01:11.273
You and I both have lots of friends

00:01:11.273 --> 00:01:13.442
who've achieved everything they
could ever have dreamed of,

00:01:13.442 --> 00:01:14.275
and they're miserable.

00:01:14.275 --> 00:01:15.725
I get the phone call to
help turn them around.

00:01:15.725 --> 00:01:17.379
They're missing a meaningful life

00:01:17.379 --> 00:01:18.742
and meaning comes from two things.

00:01:18.742 --> 00:01:21.007
I always tell people
happiness comes from progress.

00:01:21.007 --> 00:01:23.043
If you can do something
where you're growing

00:01:23.043 --> 00:01:25.154
and because you've grown
you have something to give

00:01:25.154 --> 00:01:26.708
to other people that's meaningful,

00:01:26.708 --> 00:01:28.697
insight, love, caring, something,

00:01:28.697 --> 00:01:29.881
then life is rich.

00:01:29.881 --> 00:01:31.290
Because happiness comes and goes.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.554
Happiness is not here every moment

00:01:32.554 --> 00:01:34.940
and happiness isn't all
it's cracked up to be.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:35.961
Meaning is.

00:01:35.961 --> 00:01:37.907
There are people that have
gone through horrible times.

00:01:37.907 --> 00:01:39.807
I met a woman who is 109 years old

00:01:39.807 --> 00:01:41.936
and she was in the concentration camps,

00:01:41.936 --> 00:01:43.817
and is the oldest-living
Holocaust survivor.

00:01:43.817 --> 00:01:46.410
And that woman's life is so
rich because of all the pain,

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:49.223
because she's used that to help
other people, still at 109.

00:01:49.223 --> 00:01:51.282
She's strong, you know,
she shares her music.

00:01:51.282 --> 00:01:53.548
She does the things
that make her feel like

00:01:53.548 --> 00:01:54.381
she's got a contribution.

00:01:54.381 --> 00:01:56.548
So 109, she's fully alive.

00:01:59.857 --> 00:02:01.743
- Who did you help?

00:02:01.743 --> 00:02:05.766
I mean, I really believe
that what life is truly about

00:02:05.766 --> 00:02:07.867
is making other people happier.

00:02:07.867 --> 00:02:10.246
And I know that sounds very obvious,

00:02:10.246 --> 00:02:12.334
but this does apply to
you as an entrepreneur,

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:14.157
or as a leader, or as a high-performer,

00:02:14.157 --> 00:02:17.276
or as someone who wants
to play at world-class.

00:02:17.276 --> 00:02:19.198
I mean, I really believe in this concept

00:02:19.198 --> 00:02:20.807
of servant leadership.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:23.074
And as I've studied
the great entrepreneurs

00:02:23.074 --> 00:02:26.344
and the great business builders
and the great humanitarians,

00:02:26.344 --> 00:02:27.710
here's what I've realized.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:30.695
Inside, sometimes it was very private,

00:02:30.695 --> 00:02:32.548
on this second point
of the purpose of life,

00:02:32.548 --> 00:02:36.715
they had this acute obsession
with delivering value

00:02:37.735 --> 00:02:40.944
and helping as many people as possible.

00:02:40.944 --> 00:02:42.263
And I really do believe

00:02:42.263 --> 00:02:44.529
that's the secondary purpose of life.

00:02:44.529 --> 00:02:46.250
It's about helping others.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:50.576
Being radically helpful to
as many people as possible.

00:02:50.576 --> 00:02:51.849
And here's the thing.

00:02:51.849 --> 00:02:53.906
If you've done the interior work,

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:58.632
so you are so full there's
no holes within you,

00:02:58.632 --> 00:03:01.568
then you're not going to
be a taker from the world,

00:03:01.568 --> 00:03:02.789
you're going to be a giver.

00:03:02.789 --> 00:03:03.839
And I'm going to repeat that again.

00:03:03.839 --> 00:03:05.391
If you look at the greatest among us,

00:03:05.391 --> 00:03:07.893
they were not takers, they were givers.

00:03:07.893 --> 00:03:09.851
And here's why I think they were givers.

00:03:09.851 --> 00:03:13.369
They didn't have any needs from within.

00:03:13.369 --> 00:03:16.288
They had so fallen in
love with their greatness

00:03:16.288 --> 00:03:19.292
and their peace and their
joy and their potential

00:03:19.292 --> 00:03:22.115
that they didn't need
to take from the world,

00:03:22.115 --> 00:03:25.450
they didn't need to
take from other people.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:28.924
Their well of wisdom and compassion

00:03:28.924 --> 00:03:31.766
and self-worth was so full

00:03:31.766 --> 00:03:33.991
that they walked out into their workplace,

00:03:33.991 --> 00:03:35.622
they walked out into their industries,

00:03:35.622 --> 00:03:37.889
they walked out into their communities,

00:03:37.889 --> 00:03:39.846
and they were giving.

00:03:39.846 --> 00:03:41.456
And this applies to you
as a business builder

00:03:41.456 --> 00:03:43.141
because the more value you give,

00:03:43.141 --> 00:03:46.369
the more money you'll make,
the more your brand will fly,

00:03:46.369 --> 00:03:49.658
the more customers will beat
a path to your doorstep.

00:03:49.658 --> 00:03:51.254
And for you as a humanitarian,

00:03:51.254 --> 00:03:53.569
and you might not think of
yourself as a humanitarian,

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:56.362
but a humanitarian is simply someone

00:03:56.362 --> 00:03:58.529
that cares about humanity.

00:04:00.117 --> 00:04:03.045
And as a humanitarian, the more you give,

00:04:03.045 --> 00:04:06.005
the more you will open up
the doorways to receive

00:04:06.005 --> 00:04:08.239
from the rest of the world.

00:04:08.239 --> 00:04:10.832
- If you live in your gift,
you find your purpose.

00:04:10.832 --> 00:04:13.747
The two greatest days of your
life is the day you were born

00:04:13.747 --> 00:04:16.205
and the day you discover why.

00:04:16.205 --> 00:04:18.807
And it ain't too old to discover why.

00:04:18.807 --> 00:04:20.675
See, Kentucky Fried Chicken.

00:04:20.675 --> 00:04:22.316
You ever notice the picture of that man

00:04:22.316 --> 00:04:24.104
up there on that wall?

00:04:24.104 --> 00:04:24.937
He old.

00:04:26.316 --> 00:04:29.730
You know, that ain't the
picture of him when he was 20.

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:31.927
That's the picture of him when he hit.

00:04:31.927 --> 00:04:35.809
See, Kentucky Colonel been
frying that chicken all his life.

00:04:35.809 --> 00:04:38.692
It ain't hit 'til he was 68-years-old.

00:04:38.692 --> 00:04:39.862
So, what you trippin' for?

00:04:39.862 --> 00:04:41.787
'Cause you 50, you 55?

00:04:41.787 --> 00:04:44.354
You don't know when God going
to flip the script for you.

00:04:44.354 --> 00:04:45.587
But you can't give up.

00:04:45.587 --> 00:04:47.208
But you got to be doing your gift.

00:04:47.208 --> 00:04:49.756
Don't quit going to work,
man, without doing your gift.

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:52.042
And some of you all fry
chicken better than anybody,

00:04:52.042 --> 00:04:54.280
some of you all bake pie,
some of you all do hair,

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:56.900
some of you do makeup, some of
you all work with your hands,

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.207
some of you all cut grass,
some of you all teach better,

00:04:59.207 --> 00:05:00.768
some of you all network better.

00:05:00.768 --> 00:05:02.498
That's your gift, go do that.

00:05:02.498 --> 00:05:05.040
Go do that, what you
driving to work for everyday

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.365
and you ain't happy with yourself?

00:05:06.365 --> 00:05:07.757
Why, 'cause you got bills?

00:05:07.757 --> 00:05:10.790
You going to have bills,
I don't care what you do.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.081
What you going to mess your credit up?

00:05:13.081 --> 00:05:15.055
Then you can't buy nothing no how.

00:05:15.055 --> 00:05:17.326
- That you know while we are all unique,

00:05:17.326 --> 00:05:19.305
we all share similarities.

00:05:19.305 --> 00:05:22.734
All human cultures across the span of time

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:27.136
have been found to truly value
very simple, basic things.

00:05:27.136 --> 00:05:31.086
You know, love, truth,
fairness, freedom, unity,

00:05:31.086 --> 00:05:34.023
respect, responsibility, and tolerance.

00:05:34.023 --> 00:05:36.178
And as we recognize those,

00:05:36.178 --> 00:05:38.270
now not all of them exuded it great,

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.415
but as a part of their culture,

00:05:40.415 --> 00:05:41.727
there was the operating norm

00:05:41.727 --> 00:05:43.209
that valued those types of things.

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:44.571
Something connects us.

00:05:44.571 --> 00:05:48.238
It's a human fabric of
values and of beliefs

00:05:49.219 --> 00:05:53.386
that usually center around
caring and compassion and love

00:05:54.786 --> 00:05:56.829
and truth with one another

00:05:56.829 --> 00:05:58.885
because that's what keeps us all together.

00:05:58.885 --> 00:06:01.692
And that is what not only
helped us survive at one point,

00:06:01.692 --> 00:06:04.852
but more importantly, it made
us feel spiritually fulfilled.

00:06:04.852 --> 00:06:06.352
Love is a purpose.

00:06:08.261 --> 00:06:11.190
Love has been argued to be the purpose

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:13.914
by a whole lot more smart
and intelligent persons

00:06:13.914 --> 00:06:16.286
than the guy you're
listening to right now,

00:06:16.286 --> 00:06:17.725
I can tell you that.

00:06:17.725 --> 00:06:20.135
But if that's true,

00:06:20.135 --> 00:06:22.802
if connection, love is so vital,

00:06:24.225 --> 00:06:25.924
how are we doing in those categories?

00:06:25.924 --> 00:06:28.325
Are we living purposefully
with the people around us?

00:06:28.325 --> 00:06:30.351
Or are we even sensing and seeing them

00:06:30.351 --> 00:06:33.917
so that we can connect with
them and live out that purpose

00:06:33.917 --> 00:06:36.844
and sense that purpose by really
connecting with the people

00:06:36.844 --> 00:06:38.716
that we truly love and adore?

00:06:38.716 --> 00:06:40.407
A lot of people are so distracted today,

00:06:40.407 --> 00:06:42.597
they can barely even look
at somebody in the eye

00:06:42.597 --> 00:06:43.945
when they walk down the street.

00:06:43.945 --> 00:06:45.498
You know, they're looking,
I don't like this.

00:06:45.498 --> 00:06:47.110
They can't even pay
attention to their spouse

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.964
or their lover when they
walk into the house.

00:06:48.964 --> 00:06:51.933
I mean, they're distracted,
they are detached,

00:06:51.933 --> 00:06:55.606
and they are dissipating in life energy

00:06:55.606 --> 00:06:58.304
because they are not giving and receiving

00:06:58.304 --> 00:06:59.922
that incredible energy
that can only happen

00:06:59.922 --> 00:07:01.610
between two human beings.

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:05.488
And so we have to ask how are
we doing in our relationships

00:07:05.488 --> 00:07:08.392
and could we give more
purpose to those relationships

00:07:08.392 --> 00:07:12.237
so they can sense more purpose in life?

00:07:12.237 --> 00:07:14.642
- I don't think you determine
what your purpose is,

00:07:14.642 --> 00:07:16.797
I think you discover what your purpose is.

00:07:16.797 --> 00:07:18.046
There's a difference.

00:07:18.046 --> 00:07:20.629
Determining indicates deciding.

00:07:23.549 --> 00:07:25.293
And I don't think you decide.

00:07:25.293 --> 00:07:27.338
I think if you go about it the right way,

00:07:27.338 --> 00:07:29.106
you discover it.

00:07:29.106 --> 00:07:32.870
Like, there's some people that
should be painting all day.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:34.902
They're great artists.

00:07:34.902 --> 00:07:38.412
Like Michelangelo was
obviously a great artist,

00:07:38.412 --> 00:07:39.829
a great sculptor.

00:07:41.046 --> 00:07:43.379
I mean, that was his purpose

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:46.320
in his life.

00:07:47.175 --> 00:07:51.958
Well, I believe my purpose
is doing what I'm doing.

00:07:51.958 --> 00:07:55.186
Your purpose is why you get
out of bed in the morning.

00:07:55.186 --> 00:07:56.817
Do you know why you get up?

00:07:56.817 --> 00:07:58.707
Well, most people say,
"Well, it's to go to work."

00:07:58.707 --> 00:08:01.786
Well, that'd be a good
reason to stay in bed.

00:08:01.786 --> 00:08:03.835
You say, "Well, everybody's doing it."

00:08:03.835 --> 00:08:05.556
That'd be another reason to stay in bed.

00:08:05.556 --> 00:08:07.162
If you're ever doing
what everybody's doing,

00:08:07.162 --> 00:08:09.999
you're probably going
in the wrong direction.

00:08:09.999 --> 00:08:13.444
Your purpose is your reason for living.

00:08:13.444 --> 00:08:16.133
What you want to do is sit down

00:08:16.133 --> 00:08:18.633
and maybe take a pen and a pad

00:08:21.387 --> 00:08:24.797
and then ask yourself, "What
do I really love doing?"

00:08:24.797 --> 00:08:27.032
Now, you may have to
spend a while at this.

00:08:27.032 --> 00:08:30.699
You might get up an
hour early every morning

00:08:31.798 --> 00:08:34.247
and go sit under a tree somewhere

00:08:34.247 --> 00:08:37.233
if you're in a nice climate

00:08:37.233 --> 00:08:38.596
or pick a favorite chair,

00:08:38.596 --> 00:08:41.483
some place where you're
not going to be disturbed.

00:08:41.483 --> 00:08:43.650
And totally relax and say,

00:08:45.948 --> 00:08:49.656
"If I could spend my life doing something,

00:08:49.656 --> 00:08:52.156
"what do I really love doing?"

00:08:54.282 --> 00:08:56.595
Now, since you don't ask
yourself that question everyday,

00:08:56.595 --> 00:08:58.709
it might take a while for this answer

00:08:58.709 --> 00:09:00.227
to come to the surface,

00:09:00.227 --> 00:09:03.916
but it comes to your consciousness.

00:09:03.916 --> 00:09:05.101
And it may take a while.

00:09:05.101 --> 00:09:09.301
You may have to do this every
morning for three months,

00:09:09.301 --> 00:09:13.467
but it would be well-invested, the time.

00:09:13.467 --> 00:09:14.855
- What lights you up in the morning?

00:09:14.855 --> 00:09:17.281
What would get you up
early and keep you up late?

00:09:17.281 --> 00:09:20.561
Ask questions like, "If I
could only spend my life

00:09:20.561 --> 00:09:23.851
"doing one thing, what would it be?

00:09:23.851 --> 00:09:27.808
"If I had to actually pay
to do something as a job,

00:09:27.808 --> 00:09:29.283
"what would it be?"

00:09:29.283 --> 00:09:31.071
And start getting in touch
with that part of you

00:09:31.071 --> 00:09:34.467
that is compelled to do things
that align with your truth,

00:09:34.467 --> 00:09:36.862
rather than fit somebody else's pictures

00:09:36.862 --> 00:09:38.068
or run after somebody else's dreams

00:09:38.068 --> 00:09:40.057
and help them achieve their goals,

00:09:40.057 --> 00:09:42.439
which, unfortunately, most people do.

00:09:42.439 --> 00:09:45.355
So, once you've found
out what your passion is,

00:09:45.355 --> 00:09:49.587
the next step to deepen that
is to get a big enough why.

00:09:49.587 --> 00:09:51.895
Not a what, a why.

00:09:51.895 --> 00:09:53.402
Why is it you're doing this?

00:09:53.402 --> 00:09:55.727
Because, again, if it's to get approval,

00:09:55.727 --> 00:09:58.498
if it's to get significance,
if it's to be liked or loved,

00:09:58.498 --> 00:10:01.349
that's very shallow and very short-term.

00:10:01.349 --> 00:10:03.731
And it's a hamster wheel
to nowhere for most people.

00:10:03.731 --> 00:10:05.820
Instead, the people who
are the most passionate,

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:07.676
the people that have the biggest why's

00:10:07.676 --> 00:10:11.810
usually focus on something
that is beyond themselves.

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:13.797
Do you have somebody you love

00:10:13.797 --> 00:10:15.185
that you want to provide a future for

00:10:15.185 --> 00:10:17.506
that you can share together

00:10:17.506 --> 00:10:19.642
that comes from abundance nor scarcity?

00:10:19.642 --> 00:10:21.360
Do you want to be able
to provide opportunities

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:23.786
for your children that you never had?

00:10:23.786 --> 00:10:25.954
Do you want to create a
mark and leave a legacy

00:10:25.954 --> 00:10:28.761
in your community or your country

00:10:28.761 --> 00:10:31.896
that most people will never be able to do?

00:10:31.896 --> 00:10:34.483
That takes a level of
commitment and courage

00:10:34.483 --> 00:10:36.602
that serves beyond our own ego.

00:10:36.602 --> 00:10:38.221
You get in touch with that part of you,

00:10:38.221 --> 00:10:42.384
the dream, the truth that
you were born to do and be,

00:10:42.384 --> 00:10:46.551
and I guarantee you, passion
will not be far behind.

00:10:48.187 --> 00:10:49.993
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:10:49.993 --> 00:10:51.982
I'd love to know what did
you think of this video,

00:10:51.982 --> 00:10:53.083
what did you take from it,

00:10:53.083 --> 00:10:55.431
if you're going to immediately
apply it to your life

00:10:55.431 --> 00:10:56.975
or to your business somehow.

00:10:56.975 --> 00:10:59.513
Please share, leave it
down in the comments below.

00:10:59.513 --> 00:11:02.150
I'm really excited to
see what you have to say.

